<title>PHILIPPINES: Alaska says 9-mth net slides 65 percent.</title>
<headline>Alaska says 9-mth net slides 65 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>	    (in million pesos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (pesos)   0.063 vs 0.176</p>
<p>    Net Sales (billion)	    1.621 vs 1.548</p>
<p>    Net income			    60 vs 170</p>
<p>Note: Full name Alaska Milk Corp. Earnings per shares were adjusted for a 50 percent dividend. The company said its operating expenses in the first nine months of the year increased by 15 percent year-on-year to 1.52 billion pesos from 1.32 billion in the same 1995 period largely due to higher raw material costs, particularly skimmed milk powder.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
